  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mauritius constituents implement policies and programmes for decent and productive work in the green and blue economy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mauritius is taking steps to ensure safe and fair working conditions, particularly in the maritime sector. The country is focusing on:

Improving workplace safety: Implementing stricter safety standards for docks, fishing vessels, and fish processing facilities.
Training workers: Equipping workers with essential skills like first aid and firefighting.
Strengthening institutions: Enhancing the capacity of government agencies to enforce labor laws and regulations.
Monitoring and reporting: Tracking workplace accidents and implementing corrective measures.
Transition to a green economy: Promoting sustainable practices in the maritime sector and creating green jobs.
By prioritizing worker safety and environmental sustainability, Mauritius aims to build a stronger and more resilient economy.</narrative>
  </description>
